                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Probably the best Fallout game ever.\n\nIt experiments with Fallout as a franchise, rather than simply trying to be another Fallout RPG.\n\nAnd it works brilliantly. It's an amazing squad-based tactical game that introduces new lore concepts and has had a significant influence on later entries, including Fallout: New Vegas, Fallout 4, and the Fallout TV series.\n\nFrom the Brotherhood's airships, which would later find their spiritual successor in the Prydwen, to splinter factions, militaristic expansionism, and the concept of hidden control vaults, Fallout Tactics explored ideas that would become increasingly prominent throughout the franchise. Even Caesar's Legion bears striking thematic similarities to the Midwestern Brotherhood's model of military conquest and political domination.\n\nThe Brotherhood of Steel is exceptionally well-written, and the world is thrilling and remarkably believable from both anthropological and political perspectives. Unlike the more isolationist portrayals of the Brotherhood, the Midwestern chapter behaves like an emerging military state, absorbing communities, recruiting outsiders, and expanding its influence across the wasteland.\n\nThe gameplay still feels fantastic today. It's responsive, engaging, and surprisingly accessible despite its age. The game is also incredibly lightweight and will run on almost any modern computer.\n\nFallout Tactics deserves far more recognition than it gets.\n\n(Also, OBJECTIVELY the coolest Power Armor design in the entire franchise comes from this game.)",
